    <comment>New package: soapy-airspyhf - SoapySDR backend for Airspy HF+ receivers

WHAT
Exposes Airspy HF+ / Discovery receivers through the vendor-neutral SoapySDR
API. Ships exactly one dlopen'd plugin,
%{_libdir}/SoapySDR/modules0.8-3/libairspyhfSupport.so, in subpackage
soapysdr0.8-3-module-airspyhf. No shared library, no headers, no -devel.

LICENCE
MIT, single-licensed. Upstream LICENSE.txt is packaged via %license and every
source file carries the same MIT header. Nothing bundled or vendored.

WHY FACTORY
Factory already ships soapy-sdr plus seven SoapySDR backends - soapy-airspy,
soapy-bladerf, soapy-hackrf, soapy-osmo, soapy-remote, soapy-rtlsdr and
soapy-uhd - and every one of them, like this package, is developed in
hardware:sdr. This is a direct peer of that set: Factory has soapy-airspy for
the Airspy R2/Mini but nothing for the HF+ family.

More concretely, Factory already ships the device library airspyhf 1.6.8 (also
from hardware:sdr) and no Factory package currently uses it. Without this
module that library has no SoapySDR backend to reach it, so an Airspy HF+
cannot be driven from SoapySDR applications - gnuradio and welle-io both build
against SoapySDR in Factory, and soapy-remote re-exports any module over the
network.

VERSION - a pinned snapshot, deliberately
0.2.0+git20251009.7457d69. Upstream has cut only two tags ever (0.1.0 in
2018, 0.2.0 in 2021). Master carries three commits past that tag, and they
matter:
 - Gain detection moved from a nested AIRSPYHF_VER_* macro cascade to cmake
   check_function_exists(airspyhf_set_hf_att). The old cascade demanded
   REVISION &gt;= 2 regardless of MINOR. Every released libairspyhf from 1.1.2
   onwards satisfies that, 1.6.8 included, so this is not a live breakage in
   Factory today - but airspyhf master is 1.8.1 (MINOR=8, REVISION=1), which
   the cascade silently fails. The capability probe is correct by construction
   rather than by coincidence.
 - cmake_minimum_required widened to a 2.8.12...3.10 range. That range is what
   lets this configure under Factory's cmake 4.4 without the
   -DCMAKE_POLICY_VERSION_MINIMUM=3.5 workaround Factory's soapy-airspy still
   carries.
Fedora Rawhide ships this identical commit (soapy-airspyhf
0.2.0^20251009git7457d69-2.fc45), independent corroboration of the pin. The version uses '+git' rather than '~git'
so that it sorts above 0.2.0; soapy-sdr and soapy-uhd in Factory already use
the same snapshot convention. Sources come from a pinned-commit obs_scm
_service, so the snapshot is reproducible.

BUILD
Clean. rpmlint reports 0 errors and 0 badness; the only warning is
no-%check-section, which is accurate - upstream ships no test suite.

pluskalm has been added as package maintainer in hardware:sdr.

ADDED IN THIS REVISION
Explicit &quot;Requires: soapy-sdr&quot; on the module subpackage, at dimstar's request
on SR 1374694 (soapy-plutosdr), applied to all five plugin submissions: &quot;Shouldn't that require soapy-sdr? The module
on its own seems quite useless&quot;.

To be precise about what this does and does not change: the dlopen itself lives
in libSoapySDR (SoapySDR::loadModules(), reached from Device::make()), which the
module already pulled in through its automatic soname dependency on
libSoapySDR.so.0.8-3 - so any application linking the library could always load
the module. What nothing pulled in was the soapy-sdr package, which ships
SoapySDRUtil; the module could therefore be installed on a system with no
SoapySDR client at all to enumerate or probe it. So this is a usability
dependency rather than a functional one, and the spec comment says so. The
soname dependency remains the ABI-exact constraint, which is why the new line is
deliberately unversioned instead of duplicating the ABI in the spec.

Stated plainly so it is not mistaken for convention: none of Factory's existing
SoapySDR plugins - soapy-airspy, soapy-bladerf, soapy-hackrf, soapy-osmo,
soapy-remote, soapy-rtlsdr, soapy-uhd - carries such a Requires. This change
makes these five stricter than current Factory practice; it is what the reviewer
asked for, not a convention being matched.

Rebuilt natively on aarch64 after the change: green, rpmlint unchanged, and
&quot;rpm -qp --requires&quot; on the built module now lists both
libSoapySDR.so.0.8-3()(64bit) and soapy-sdr.

Supersedes SR 1374702.</comment>
